From e2fbde80b361479aec65e7e254910f6b18d41dbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:13:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] media: camss: connect SM8550 C-PHY endpoints and stream
 lifecycle

Bind an explicit link frequency to a calibrated settle counter and validate raw trio properties before the generic endpoint parser. Route legacy C-PHY streaming through the PHY 2.1.2 backend and clean up receivers when a later pipeline start fails.

Cover endpoint rejection, repeated C-PHY and D-PHY register programming, and real V4L2 graph startup cleanup. V4L2 intentionally logs and suppresses stop errors, so cleanup success is not hardware halt proof.
---
